{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P15018","secondaryAccessions":["B2RCW7","B5MC23","Q52LZ2"],"uniProtkbId":"LIF_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1990-04-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1990-04-01","entryVersion":229,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"3143918"}],"value":"Leukemia inhibitory factor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"3143918"}],"value":"LIF"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2475312"}],"value":"Differentiation-stimulating factor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2475312"}],"value":"D factor"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2730639"}],"value":"Melanoma-derived LPL inhibitor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2730639"}],"value":"MLPLI"}]}],"innNames":[{"value":"Emfilermin"}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:6596"}],"value":"LIF"},"synonyms":[{"value":"HILDA"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P09056"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P17777"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11294841"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14527405"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"36930708"}],"value":"Functions as a cytokine that binds to the LIF receptor complex (PubMed:11294841, PubMed:14527405, PubMed:36930708). The LIF receptor complex indeed consists of two signaling receptor subunits IL6ST/gp130 and LIFR that transduce the signal into the cell (PubMed:14527405, PubMed:36930708). Functionally, regulates cell self-renewal, differentiation and survival of embryonic stem cells (ESCs) and is crucial for embryonic implantation (By similarity). Mechanistically, ligand binding to LIFR, induces heterodimerization with IL6ST/gp130 activating JAK tyrosine kinases (JAK1 or JAK2 and to a lesser extent TYK2) bound to their intracellular domains (PubMed:11294841). These kinases subsequently phosphorylate IL6ST/gp130 and LIFR (PubMed:11294841). The tyrosine phosphorylated signaling receptors serve in turn as docking sites for recruitment and activation of signal transducers and activators of transcription (STAT3 and to lesser extent STAT1) (PubMed:11294841). In parallel to the activation of the STAT3-pathway, the binding of LIF to the LIF receptor complex leads to the activation of the mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK) and the phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI(3)K) pathways (PubMed:11294841). Tyrosine phosphorylation of the p85 subunit of PI(3)K by JAK1 leads to activation of the serine/ threonine kinase AKT (protein kinase B) (PubMed:11294841). PI(3)K-dependent signaling is required for efficient self-renewal of murine ES cells, and regulation of ERK activity is functionally important in this response (By similarity). Moreover, induces tyrosine phosphorylation of PTPN11, that associates with IL6ST/gp130-LIFR, which in turn recruits the p85 regulatory subunit of PI(3)K protein kinase, promoting PI3K-AKT activation, and GRB2-RAS-MAPK signaling (PubMed:11294841)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P15018","intActId":"EBI-1037189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O60760","geneName":"HPGDS","intActId":"EBI-10187349"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P15018","intActId":"EBI-1037189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P40189","geneName":"IL6ST","intActId":"EBI-1030834"},"numberOfExperiments":4,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P15018","intActId":"EBI-1037189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q15323","geneName":"KRT31","intActId":"EBI-948001"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P15018","intActId":"EBI-1037189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P60328","geneName":"KRTAP12-3","intActId":"EBI-11953334"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P15018","intActId":"EBI-1037189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P61601","geneName":"NCALD","intActId":"EBI-749635"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"11294841"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"commentType":"ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS","events":["Alternative splicing"],"isoforms":[{"name":{"value":"1"},"isoformIds":["P15018-1"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Displayed"},{"name":{"value":"2"},"isoformIds":["P15018-2"],"sequenceIds":["VSP_045551","VSP_045552"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Described"}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14527405"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"36930708"}],"value":"At the structural level composed of a canonical four-helix bundle structure in which four major helices (termed helices A to D) are linked by three loops (termed AB, BC, and CD loops), as well as three conserved receptor binding epitopes (termed sites 1 to 3) (PubMed:36930708). Sites 2 and 3 bind to IL6ST/gp130 and LIFR, respectively, while site 1 is left empty (PubMed:36930708). Initiation of assembly proceeds with LIF binding through its site 3 interface to the Ig domain of LIFR (PubMed:14527405). IL6ST is then recruited to this heterodimeric complex and binds to the site 2 of LIF forming a heterotrimer with one copy each of LIF, IL6ST and LIFR (PubMed:14527405)"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"value":"In phase II clinical trial. The drug is being developed by Amrad to assist embryo implantation in women who have failed to become pregnant despite assisted reproductive technologies (ART)"}],"commentType":"PHARMACEUTICAL"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the LIF/OSM family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"commentType":"WEB RESOURCE","resourceName":"Wikipedia","resourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leukemia_inhibitory_factor","ftp":false,"note":"Leukemia inhibitory factor entry"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":22,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"2730639"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":23,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":202,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Leukemia inhibitory factor","featureId":"PRO_0000017715"},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":31,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":31,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8489250"}],"featureId":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":56,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":56,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8489250"}],"featureId":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":85,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":85,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","so